# Code practices

Prefer existing modules in `config/` and `services/` over a one-off. If you
add a custom option, document it in `docs/custom-options.md`. Patterns live in
`docs/standards.md`; do not invent a parallel one.

**Secrets never enter the Nix store.** No `initialAdminPassword`, no password
string in a Nix attr, no `environment.FOO = "secret"`. Inject with
`sops.templates` + systemd `EnvironmentFile`, `$__file{}`, or a runtime read.
See `docs/secrets.md` and `docs/how-to-manage-secrets.md`. Per-host files:
`inventory-secrets.mdc`.

**Do not busy-wait.** Use `fleet.waitForHost` or `fleet.waitFor.postgres`.
TCP probe with timeout, not a ping loop in the service script.

**Do not hardcode Tailscale IPs.** Resolve `tailscale0` at unit start into an
`EnvironmentFile`. See `docs/how-to-dynamic-tailscale.md`.

Deployed-host `nix.conf` lists `https://cache.nixos.org`. Do not put
Attic back. Freeze: `infrastructure.mdc`.

Never commit `ansible/.vault_pass.txt` or copy that pattern into flake secrets.

Match neighbouring code. Do not add a dependency, language, or helper without
a flake input or `packages.` entry the rest of the tree can build.
